  "openapi": "3.1.0",
  "info": {
    "title": "IM Group and Conversation Snapshot API",
    "version": "1.0.0",
    "description": "Canonical additive group contract. HTTPS only; credentials only Authorization Bearer, never query/body/cookie/logs/errors. Core validates current database Session ID/epoch/client type/revocation/expiry for every call including replay. Reject unknown or repeated query parameters, JSON duplicate fields, non-JSON or bodies above 16384 UTF-8 bytes. Mutation precedence: reject query or undecodable JSON; authenticate; validate exact body/path; validate GROUP and active actor membership for add; validate every target's friendship to actor, including already-active members; then compare existing receipt and either replay original status/body or return conflict; otherwise one Core transaction commits all effects. Current Session/authorization must remain valid at commit, including when a call waited on locks. Target UUID text uses canonical lowercase hyphenated representation; sort/distinct before operation comparison; raw target array length 1..100, actor rejected, at least one distinct target. No partial success. Create automatically adds actor as OWNER; targets MEMBER. Any effective member may add its own friends, independent of OWNER/creator/other members' friendship. Missing conversation, DIRECT, non-member, nonexistent/nonfriend target and mixed invalid batch all return 403 AUTHORIZATION_DENIED without revealing which target; self/shape errors return 400. Replays check current authorization but never mutate or rederive original results from current membership. CREATE always returns original 201; ADD original 200 with only actual new IDs, possibly empty. Result IDs sorted unique; CREATE includes actor, ADD excludes actor. createdAt is the original durable operation record timestamp, not a pre-COMMIT acknowledgement or measured commit completion time. Same request UUID may be reused across distinct actor/type/conversation scopes. Any definite failure rolls back all new business/receipt/user-Sync/outbox effects. Unknown commit/timeout/response loss is unconfirmed; retry original identity and targets. Unexpected server errors propagate as non-2xx transport failures, never successful empty output or an invented catalog code. Every actual membership change invalidates all current effective members including newly added users through existing conversation.changed/membership.changed and matching Outbox in the same transaction; no duplicate logical event for replay/already-member. New members can read existing committed group messages under current member authorization, no join-seq rule. Success and catalog errors echo a decoded valid mutation body requestId or GET requestId; otherwise use a fresh server UUID. All responses no-store; no credentials in output. Existing DIRECT/Auth/WSS/ACK/Sync contracts and old-client window unchanged. Existing0001 GROUP rows continue to be readable/sendable and may receive new authorized ADD operations. If an existing CREATE identity has no verifiable original receipt, both old receipt-less GROUP state and an unexpected missing new receipt must fail the new POST with a non-2xx server failure retaining the missing persisted original-result cause. Do not invent a canonical ErrorResponse, infer different targets and return409, guess original results, backfill a success receipt or overwrite the group. Earlier no public group-create HTTP endpoint existed, so this unreplayable state does not remove any old HTTP success behavior. Only a verified existing receipt with a different normalized target set establishes409 GROUP_REQUEST_CONFLICT; new atomic HTTP operations replay their recorded original result exactly."
  },
